tao — keeper's patched copy
===========================

This directory is tao 0.35.3, the window and event-loop layer under Tauri, as
crates.io serves it, with one change. It is used through `[patch.crates-io]` in
`src-tauri/Cargo.toml`.

  upstream: https://github.com/tauri-apps/tao
  copied from: the crates.io package tao 0.35.3 (checksum
               d1c93047acf68669466a34690ac58cca7010bd1b201e1ec86f1fd0a75d3dd4a9)
  license: Apache-2.0 (LICENSE and LICENSE.spdx, unchanged)

The change
----------

`src/platform_impl/ios/app_state.rs`, `connect_scene`: the first scene's
`UISceneConnectionOptions.URLContexts` are emitted as `Event::Opened`.
`src/platform_impl/ios/scene.rs`: the URL parsing that `scene:openURLContexts:`
already did moves into `urls_of`, shared by both.

Why: iOS 27 refuses to launch an app that has not adopted the UIScene lifecycle,
so keeper declares a scene manifest. In that lifecycle a URL that launched the
app is delivered only in the first scene's connection options — not to
`application:openURL:options:` and not to `scene:openURLContexts:` — and tao
through 0.37.1 never reads them, so a `keeper://setup?…` code scanned while
keeper was closed would open keeper and do nothing.

Retiring it
-----------

When upstream tao reads the first scene's URL contexts, delete the
`[patch.crates-io]` table and this directory, and re-run the cold-launch check
in docs/ios.md.
